//www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqwy06zrd26lo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss","source_type":"live","vocabPoints":[{"word":"disappointing","phonetic":"","definition":"a. 使失望的, 期待落空的, 令人沮丧的","example":"The UK&#x27;s Energy Secretary, Miatta Fahnbulleh, described the failure to reach a political agreement as immensely disappointing .","example2":"Experts are concerned about the disappointing change in policy.","en_def":"s. not up to expectations"},{"word":"international","phonetic":"","definition":"国际的","example":"And COP31 was the first annual UN conference to formally discuss how one of the key international targets for limiting climate change would be missed.","example2":"The international situation has drawn widespread attention.","en_def":"any of several international socialist organizations；a. concerning or belonging to all or at least two or more nations"},{"word":"disappointed","phonetic":"","definition":"a. 失望的","example":"UN Secretary General Antonio Guterres, in his last COP before he steps down, said he was deeply disappointed .","example2":"The disappointed situation has drawn widespread attention.","en_def":"v fail to meet the hopes or expectations of；s disappointingly unsuccessful"}],"grammarPoints":[{"pattern":"被动语态 (Passive Voice)","explanation":"be 动词 + 过去分词。新闻大量使用被动语态，因为动作的承受者比执行者更重要。注意 by 短语引出真正的执行者，常被省略。","en":"The passive voice emphasizes the action or its receiver rather than the doer: be + past participle. Used heavily in news when the doer is unknown or less important. The agent can be added with 'by' or omitted entirely.","example":"After two weeks of negotiations, exhausted delegates were presented with a new, draft deal in the early hours of Sunday to try to break the deadlock.","example2":"The bridge was built in 1932 and is still used by thousands of commuters every day."}],"slangPoints":[{"term":"back down","meaning":"让步；退缩（refused to back down 拒绝让步）","en":"\"back down\" — a common English phrase; typical collocation: \"refused to back down\".","example":"Many countries say they are committed to eventually bringing warming back down to 1.5C, but that will require an ambitious ramping up of technologies - which do not yet exist at scale - to remove carbon dioxide from the ","example2":"The government refused to back down over the new tax."}]},{"id":"n1795422102_1","date":"2026-11-23","source":"BBC","country":"UK","title":"What's next after no deal at COP31 climate talks?","summary":"The talks have been the longest-running in the summit's history, with negotiations breaking down two days after they had been due to end.","body":"BBC News {\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"VideoObject\",\"name\":\"What's next after no deal at COP31 climate talks?\",\"description\":\"The talks have been the longest-running in the summit's history, with negotiations breaking down two days after they had been due to end.\",\"thumbnailUrl\":[\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/1920/galileo/p0ppcl23.jpg\",\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/1248/galileo/p0ppcl23.jpg\",\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/688/galileo/p0ppcl23.jpg\",\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/400/galileo/p0ppcl23.jpg\"],\"uploadDate\":\"2026-11-22T18:57:24.192Z\",\"duration\":\"PT1M5S\"} What&#x27;s next after no deal at COP31 climate talks? To play this video you need to enable JavaScript in your browser. This video can not be played\n\nClose The COP31 climate summit in Turkey has officially come to an end after countries failed to come to a consensus on a new deal.\n\nThe European Union and some other countries rejected a fourth draft agreement over its failure to mention a need to phase out fossil fuels, the largest driver of global climate change.\n\nTwo days of additional negotiations made it the longest talks in the summit&#x27;s history.\n\nThe failure to reach a deal triggered criticism from prominent climate advocates, including former US Vice President Al Gore, who wrote it was outrageous that a handful of petro-states have veto power over any mention of fossil fuels .\n\nBBC climate and science reporter Esme Stallard reports from Antalya, in Turkey.\n\nShare close panel Share page Copy link About sharing Read description Explore more What&#x27;s next after no deal at COP31 climate talks? Video, 00:01:05 What&#x27;s next after no deal at COP31 climate talks?\n\n1:05 Up Next. Will COP31 end with a new global climate deal? Video, 00:01:20 Will COP31 end with a new global climate deal?\n\n1:20 Editor&#x27;s recommendations &#x27;Danger seems greater all the time&#x27;: Ukrainians search for missing after Russian strikes. Video, 00:01:47 &#x27;Danger seems greater all the time&#x27;: Ukrainians search for missing after Russian strikes\n\n1:47 What the new UK-EU deal could mean for future post-Brexit relations. Video, 00:01:42 What the new UK-EU deal could mean for future post-Brexit relations\n\n1:42 Wes Streeting calls Putin a &#x27;cold-blooded killer&#x27; as he meets Zelensky in Kyiv. Video, 00:01:40 Wes Streeting calls Putin a &#x27;cold-blooded killer&#x27; as he meets Zelensky in Kyiv\n\n1:40 Cost of living protests sweep across Europe. Video, 00:01:08 Cost of living protests sweep across Europe\n\n1:08 Miami or Vice City? Tour the real-world inspiration for GTA 6. Video, 00:01:35 Miami or Vice City? Tour the real-world inspiration for GTA 6\n\n1:35 What the Brussels summit could mean for the UK-EU Brexit deal. Video, 00:00:50 What the Brussels summit could mean for the UK-EU Brexit deal\n\n0:50 BBC correspondents discuss what Trump, Xi and Putin got out of historic talks. Video, 00:02:02 BBC correspondents discuss what Trump, Xi and Putin got out of historic talks\n\n2:02 Rohingya genocide: What was said in court and what happens now? Video, 00:01:15 Rohingya genocide: What was said in court and what happens now?\n\n1:15 &#x27;You can be believed and understood&#x27;: Joanne Young speaks after verdict. Video, 00:03:07 &#x27;You can be believed and understood&#x27;: Joanne Young speaks after verdict\n\n3:07 Catherine visits Mumbai maternity hospital on the last day of royal trip. Video, 00:00:58 Catherine visits Mumbai maternity hospital on the last day of royal trip\n\n0:58 Home News Sport Earth Reel Worklife Travel Culture Future Music TV Weather Sounds Terms of Use About the BBC Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility Help Parental Guidance Contact the BBC Careers BBC emails for you Advertise with us Copyright © 2026 BBC. The BBC is not responsible for the content of external sites. Read about our approach to external linking.","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cr1ewge81q4qo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss","source_type":"live","vocabPoints":[{"word":"correspondent","phonetic":"","definition":"n. 通讯记者, 通信者\\ / [经] 客户, 代理商行, 代理银行","example":"Video, 00:00:50 What the Brussels summit could mean for the UK-EU Brexit deal\n\n0:50 BBC correspondents discuss what Trump, Xi and Putin got out of historic talks.","example2":"Experts say correspondent will remain a central issue in the coming weeks.","en_def":"someone who communicates by means of letters；a journalist employed to provide news stories for newspapers or broadcast media"},{"word":"description","phonetic":"","definition":"描述","example":"BBC News {\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"VideoObject\",\"name\":\"What's next after no deal at COP31 climate talks?\",\"description\":\"The talks have been the longest-running in the summit's history, with negotiations","example2":"The report highlighted description as a key factor in the decision.","en_def":"a statement that represents something in words；the act of describing something"},{"word":"negotiation","phonetic":"/nɪˌɡəʊʃiˈeɪʃn/","definition":"谈判","example":"BBC News {\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"VideoObject\",\"name\":\"What's next after no deal at COP31 climate talks?\",\"description\":\"The talks have been the longest-running in the summit's history, with negotiations","_bank_example":"Negotiations resume on Tuesday.","example2":"Negotiations resume on Tuesday."}],"grammarPoints":[{"pattern":"间接引语 / 转述动词 (Reported Speech)","explanation":"said/told/warned/confirmed + that 从句（that 常省略）。新闻标题后正文常用转述动词引述当事人观点，注意从句语序不倒装。","en":"Reported (indirect) speech reports what someone said without using their exact words, typically with a reporting verb (said, told, added) and a tense shift: 'She said she was leaving.'","example":"Video, 00:02:02 BBC correspondents discuss what Trump, Xi and Putin got out of historic talks\n\n2:02 Rohingya genocide: What was said in court and what happens now?","example2":"She told reporters (that) the deal had already been signed."}],"slangPoints":[{"term":"kick off","meaning":"开始；启动（kick off a campaign）","en":"to begin or start an event or process e.g. \"The summit kicked off with a speech by the host president.\"","example":"","example2":"The summit kicked off with a speech by the host president."}]},{"id":"n1795422102_2","date":"2026-11-23","source":"BBC","country":"UK","title":"Boy, 7, pulled alive from rubble hours after Russian strike on Ukraine, rescuers say","summary":"Eleven people are dead in the attack on Dymer, with rescue efforts ongoing to find those still missing from the residential building.","body":"BBC News Boy, 7, pulled alive from rubble hours after Russian strike on Ukraine, rescuers say To play this video you need to enable JavaScript in your browser. This video can not be played\n\n&#x27;Danger seems greater all the time&#x27;: Ukrainians search for missing after Russian strikes hit Kyiv\n\nA seven-year-old boy has been rescued from the rubble of a residential building in Dymer, in the Kyiv region, after 14 hours. Overnight Russian strikes on the village killed 11 people, Ukrainian officials have said.\n\nThe attack occurred in the early hours of Sunday. A 79-year-old woman was also rescued alive from the collapsed building, Kyiv&#x27;s regional head Tymur Tkachenko said.\n\nA strike on a private home in Bila Tserkva killed one more person and set the building ablaze, he added.\n\nUkrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky also said three people were killed and 13 wounded in a separate strike on Vyshneve, also in the Kyiv region, that hit a grocery store on Sunday.\n\nUkrainian authorities said the boy in Dymer is in stable condition and was taken to hospital, and have thanked everyone involved in saving his life.\n\nZelensky and Ukraine&#x27;s national police also confirmed the rescue of the boy.\n\nIn a Telegram post, Tkachenko said the 79-year-old woman rescued from the rubble was receiving treatment in hospital.\n\nEarlier he said six people were injured in the attack, while others were still missing.\n\nImage source, Ukraine State Emergency Service Image caption, The attack on the residential building occurred in the early hours of the morning while people were asleep\n\nZelensky said more than 130 people are involved in emergency operations at the scene, and that they will continue until they have complete information about every single person .\n\nSending his condolences to the families and loved ones of those killed, he said the strike struck the residential building, practically blowing a section of it to smithereens .\n\nZelensky added that rescue efforts are complicated by constant new air raid alerts and renewed threats .\n\nThe strike hit the building at 05:00 local time, when families were still asleep, Ukraine&#x27;s minister of internal affairs Ivan Vyhivskyi said.\n\nMore than 70 strikes have been launched across 10 Ukrainian regions as of Sunday evening, Vyhivskyi added.\n\nImage source, Reuters Image caption, Emergency workers continue to search for those missing after Russian drone and missile attacks in Dymer.\n\nIn his video address posted online, Zelensky also said three people were killed and 13 injured in a strike on an ordinary grocery store in Vyshneve.\n\nMayor Illya Dikov wrote on social media that three children were among the injured.\n\nRussia also struck a power substation in the Dnipropetrovsk region, Ukraine&#x27;s Prime Minister Sergiy Koretsky said in a post on X. , external\n\nRussia launched its full-scale invasion of Ukraine in 2022.\n\nRussia-bound ship towed away after it was attacked in Gulf of Finland\n\nZelensky says Putin is a &#x27;killer&#x27; after Trump calls Russian leader a friend\n\nZelensky says Crimean Bridge strikes &#x27;fair response&#x27; as he meets UK&#x27;s Streeting\n\nThe video playlist Watch our pick of standout clips from across the BBC\n\nPrevious Next 1:32 Britain promised 7,400 homes - where are they? 00:01:32, play video Britain promised 7,400 homes - where are they? 1:05 UN climate talks end with no deal - what&#x27;s next? 00:01:05, play video UN climate talks end with no deal - what&#x27;s next? 1:12 Inside NHS&#x27;s AI breast cancer screening trial. 00:01:12, play video Inside NHS&#x27;s AI breast cancer screening trial 0:45 BBC apologises after noise disruption during Strictly. 00:00:45, play video BBC apologises after noise disruption during Strictly 1:41 Catherine&#x27;s cancer journey depicted in new documentary. 00:01:41, play video Catherine&#x27;s cancer journey depicted in new documentary 0:51 Andy Burnham must &#x27;accept Brexit&#x27; Theresa May says. 00:00:51, play video Andy Burnham must &#x27;accept Brexit&#x27; Theresa May says 1:44 Next recalls baby sleeping bag after warning from mum. 00:01:44, play video Next recalls baby sleeping bag after warning from mum 1:47 Ukrainians search for missing after Russian strikes. 00:01:47, play video Ukrainians search for missing after Russian strikes 1:10 Can lessons in eye contact prepare you for getting a job? 00:01:10, play video Can lessons in eye contact prepare you for getting a job? 1:13 Musicians being &#x27;reskinned&#x27; by AI copycats. 00:01:13, play video Musicians being &#x27;reskinned&#x27; by AI copycats 1:00 Tour the real-world inspiration for GTA 6. 00:01:00, play video Tour the real-world inspirati